message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Covenant"
version: 0.4.0
authors:
  - name: "Punarbasu"
    email: "punarbasuu@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShrewdLemon/covenant"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - model risk
  - credit risk
  - governance
  - adverse action
  - explainability
abstract: >-
  Covenant is pytest for credit-model governance. Its one original idea is
  that a model's documentation is a set of testable claims about its
  behaviour, so it tests them: git-native covenants recording a credit
  model's declared features, monotone directions, exclusions and reason-code
  method, and CI checks that fail when measured behaviour contradicts the
  claims. Covenant produces evidence; validators and auditors decide.
